        <item>
         <widget class="QFrame" name="coverage_info">
          <property name="frameShape">
           <enum>QFrame::Shape::NoFrame</enum>
          </property>
          <property name="variant" stdset="0">
           <string notr="true">info</string>
          </property>
          <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="coverage_info_layout">
           <property name="leftMargin">
            <number>14</number>
           </property>
           <property name="topMargin">
            <number>10</number>
           </property>
           <property name="rightMargin">
            <number>14</number>
           </property>
           <property name="bottomMargin">
            <number>10</number>
           </property>
           <item>
            <widget class="QLabel" name="coverage_info_label">
             <property name="text">
              <string>&lt;b&gt;How Snooz places the stages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;A sleep stage file has no times. Snooz places its stages in order, from the start of the recording.&lt;br/&gt;• The first stage goes to the first epoch (0 to 30 s), the second stage to the second epoch (30 to 60 s), and so on.&lt;br/&gt;• Every epoch needs a stage. Write Unscored for an epoch without a stage. If a stage is missing, all the stages after it are shifted.&lt;br/&gt;• If the sleep stage file has fewer stages than the recording has epochs, the last epochs keep the stage they already have in the accessory file. They are Unscored if the accessory file had no stages.&lt;br/&gt;• If the sleep stage file has more stages than the recording has epochs, it is not imported.</string>
             </property>
             <property name="textFormat">
              <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
             </property>
             <property name="wordWrap">
              <bool>true</bool>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
          </layout>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="about_import_layout">
          <property name="spacing">
           <number>6</number>
          </property>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_import_title_label">
            <property name="font">
             <font>
              <bold>true</bold>
             </font>
            </property>
            <property name="text">
             <string>About the import</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_import_label">
            <property name="text">
             <string>&lt;b&gt;Finding the sleep stage file&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Snooz finds the sleep stage file of each PSG file by its name. This name is the prefix, then the PSG file name, then the suffix, with any extension.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reading the stages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Snooz reads the stages in the chosen column. It renames each stage with its Snooz label, from the "Stage renaming" table.&lt;br/&gt;Snooz epochs last 30 s. With a shorter stage duration, Snooz keeps one stage every 30 s. For example, with a stage duration of 10 s, it keeps every third row.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Errors&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The log shows an error for a PSG file in two cases.&lt;br/&gt;• The PSG file has no sleep stage file.&lt;br/&gt;• Its sleep stage file has a label that is not in the "Stage renaming" table.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Writing the stages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Each stage becomes an event in the accessory file of the PSG file. The event has these columns.&lt;br/&gt;• group is stage.&lt;br/&gt;• name is the Snooz label, for example 2.&lt;br/&gt;• start_sec is the start of the epoch in seconds, for example 300.&lt;br/&gt;• duration_sec is 30.&lt;br/&gt;• channels is empty.&lt;br/&gt;Snooz first removes the old stages of the accessory file that have the same name as an imported stage. The other events of the accessory file are kept.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="textFormat">
             <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
             <bool>true</bool>
            </property>
            <property name="variant" stdset="0">
             <string notr="true">help</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
         </layout>
        </item>
